[2008-04-05 00:46:00] Mattisse: That got saved accidentally, with no edit summary so I will thank you properly for the Barnstar!
[2008-04-05 00:57:00] Viriditas: You're welcome.  If you are interested in bridges, dams, reservoirs, and irrigation systems, you're in luck.  There is a lot of material on that subject because of the amount of land used in Hawaii for agriculture.  In fact, if you do any research on Hawaii history at all, it would be impossible for you to ignore it!  This is especially true if you are studying [[Sugar plantations in Hawaii]].  I think you will really be interested in [[Ka Loko Reservoir]], as it is still a stub, and there is tons of good information about it in the news archives! &mdash;

